  "legal_status": "Drafting forms requiring transaction-specific Indian advocate review; not certified execution-ready legal forms.",
  "state_execution_guidance": {
    "default_state": "Tamil Nadu",
    "stamp_duty": "Determine the correct instrument classification and duty under the Indian Stamp Act, 1899 as applicable in Tamil Nadu, including Tamil Nadu amendments and current Schedule I rates. Do not apply a single flat rate to all agreements.",
    "registration": "Check the Registration Act, 1908 and Tamil Nadu amendments/rules. Registration is compulsory for specified instruments and transactions; an ordinary services agreement is not automatically registrable merely because it is signed in Tamil Nadu.",
    "adjudication": "Where classification or duty is uncertain, obtain stamp-duty adjudication/impounding advice from the competent Tamil Nadu authority before execution or reliance.",
    "execution": "Confirm e-stamping/franking/non-judicial stamp paper availability and the currently accepted execution process with the relevant Tamil Nadu authority or counsel before signing.",
    "property_documents": "If the instrument creates, declares, assigns, limits or extinguishes rights in immovable property, obtain separate property-law review for stamp duty, compulsory registration, description, schedules and local formalities.",
    "electronic_execution": "Check the Information Technology Act, 2000 and document-specific exclusions/formalities; electronic signing does not remove stamp duty or registration obligations.",
    "local_review": "State-specific rates and procedures must be verified on the execution date; this library intentionally does not hardcode stamp amounts."
  },
  "important_limitations": [
    "No stamp duty rate is hardcoded; determine instrument classification and current Tamil Nadu Schedule I rate on execution date.",
    "Registration is document- and transaction-specific; property instruments require separate review.",
    "GST/TDS, labour, sector-specific and regulatory obligations depend on facts and current law.",
    "This v2 package expands drafting structure and schedules but is not a substitute for an advocate's review."
  ]
